Skiper UI — free component use in Motion Lab

Source: https://skiper-ui.com
Author: Gxuri (https://x.com/Gur__vi)
Catalog checked: 22 October 2026, from the public components page data
(37 components marked tier "free", 69 marked tier "paid").

Component license
-----------------
Stated on https://skiper-ui.com/docs/quick-start and on each component page:

- Free to use and modify in both personal and commercial projects.
- Attribution to Skiper UI is required when using the free version.
- No attribution required with Skiper UI Pro.

This is not an OSI license. It is not MIT, Apache, or GPL. The grant is
to use and modify the free components inside a personal or commercial
project, with credit. It is not a grant to resell, sublicense, or
republish Skiper UI as a library or website.

Website terms
-------------
https://skiper-ui.com/docs/terms-of-service (updated 7 September 2025)
forbids republishing, selling, renting, sublicensing, reproducing, or
redistributing material from skiper-ui.com. That clause covers the site.
The component pages are more specific: free components may be copied into
a project with attribution. This folder follows the component grant. It
does not mirror the Skiper UI site, and it does not ship paid source.

What is included
----------------
Only free-tier components, taken from the public registry
(https://skiper-ui.com/registry/<id>.json), which does not ask for a
Pro license key. Motion is the original React, Framer Motion, GSAP, and
Swiper code, built once into motion-lab/islands.js for this static site.

Each island runs in its own document (motion-lab/preview.html) so viewport
units, sticky positioning, and scroll progress match a Skiper preview.
Lenis is attached once to that document instead of to the portfolio page.

Demo photographs and illustrations stay on skiper-ui.com and are loaded
from there. They are not copied into this repository. Credits that ship
inside the components:

- skiper30, inspired by https://www.siena.film/films/my-project-x
- skiper39, Open Peeps (https://www.openpeeps.com/) and a CodePen walk cycle
- skiper47 and skiper52, illustrations by AarzooAly (https://x.com/AarzooAly)

